// =====================================================================
// PER-MATERIAL IMPACT SOUNDS -- added 2026-08-07 with RS_Material.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// RS_Material.ImpactSound() returns one of these logical names, and the
// puff plays it. Before this, every impact in the game played a ricochet
// regardless of what was hit; these are what it plays instead.
//
// THESE ARE PLACEHOLDER MAPPINGS. There are ten generic impact lumps on
// disk and ten materials, so the groups below are subsets chosen to at
// least sound DIFFERENT from each other -- they are not authored
// per-material sets. Replacing any one of these groups with real audio
// is a pure SNDINFO edit; no code changes with it.
//
// A logical name with no lump behind it is completely silent and
// produces no error, so an unfinished group costs nothing but silence.
// =====================================================================

$random rs_impact/stone      { impact0 impact1 impact2 }
$random rs_impact/metal      { impact3 impact4 }
$random rs_impact/wood       { impact5 impact6 }
$random rs_impact/dirt       { impact7 impact8 }
$random rs_impact/glass      { impact9 impact3 }
$random rs_impact/liquid     { impact8 impact7 }

// Bodies. Organic leans on the wetter end of the set; armored and
// mechanical borrow the harder hits; energy has no good stand-in in the
// current library and is deliberately left pointing at the quietest one
// until something better is authored.
$random rs_impact/flesh      { impact5 impact8 }
$random rs_impact/armored    { impact2 impact3 }
$random rs_impact/mechanical { impact3 impact4 }
$random rs_impact/energy     { impact9 }

$volume rs_impact/stone      0.55
$volume rs_impact/metal      0.60
$volume rs_impact/wood       0.55
$volume rs_impact/dirt       0.45
$volume rs_impact/glass      0.60
$volume rs_impact/liquid     0.50
$volume rs_impact/flesh      0.50
$volume rs_impact/armored    0.55
$volume rs_impact/mechanical 0.60
$volume rs_impact/energy     0.50

// The repair tick -- plays when ten Grey Bits convert into one point of
// Condition on your equipped weapons (RS_Bits.zs, RS_Bit_Grey.TryRepair).
// It is the ONLY feedback that the automatic repair happened, since the
// owner ruled out a spend menu, so it wants to be a distinct little
// noise rather than another pickup blip. Placeholder points at the
// all-clear tone until something is authored for it.
$alias  rs_bit_repair  rs_allclear_ready
$volume rs_bit_repair  0.6

